  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile + scvi_n200 is the strongest RNA-only setup (config_005/006, ~0.65), and scvi_n200 consistently beats pca_n2000 (~0.06 gap). Image-only is very weak (0.208), so the immediate priority is maximizing the RNA branch before investing in multimodal fusion. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested scgpt, a distinct RNA foundation-model encoder, so we do not know whether it outperforms scvi_n200. Question: config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) differs from config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) only in the RNA encoder, giving a clean isolation of encoder quality in the best-performing profile setting. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It directly answers whether a different encoder family can push past the current 0.65 ceiling, which would reshape the entire search strategy. (2) avgpool is used because transformer ≈ avgpool (config_006 vs 005), so we avoid a redundant axis. (3) If scgpt is superior, we immediately know the best RNA-only baseline before any multimodal comparison; if it is not, we confirm scvi_n200 as the encoder of choice and can pivot to testing whether multimodal fusion adds value over this strong RNA-only baseline."
}

